    "title": "When do NHL playoffs start? See NHL standings, key postseason dates",
    "text": "April 15, 2026Updated April 16, 2026, 12:47 p.m. ETThe best time of the NHL season is right around the corner.Playoff hockey is almost here, as the regular season is coming to a close.History will be made this postseason in that none of the tristate trio in the New York Rangers, New Jersey Devils or New York Islanders will qualify for the Stanley Cup playoffs as all three organizations have already been eliminated from competing in the playoffs.So who's in, who's out? When will the NHL playoffs start? Which team is the odds-on-favorite to win it all?Here's what you need to know about the Stanley Cup playoffs with puck drop for the NHL postseason only a few days away:Watch NHL Stanley Cup playoffs live on SlingWhich teams are in NHL Stanley Cup playoffs? See standingsHere are the NHL standings for the Eastern and Western conferences as of Thursday, April 16.Which first round series are set for NHL playoffs?Three first round series matchups have been decided so far which include:Eastern ConferencePittsburgh Penguins (M2 vs. Philadelphia Flyers (M3): The highly anticipated Battle of Pennsylvania rivalry is renewed with the two Metropolitan Division foes going head-to-head in the playoffs for the first time since 2018.Tampa Bay Lightning (A2) vs. Montreal Canadiens (A3): A 2021 Stanley Cup Final rematch between two Atlantic Division mates.Buffalo Sabres (A1) vs. Boston Bruins (WC1): Buffalo reemerges into the playoffs for the first time in 14 seasons, winners of the Atlantic facing off against the Bruins.Carolina Hurricanes (M1) vs. Ottawa Senators (WC2): Carolina finishes with the best regular season record in the East for the fourth time in the last six seasons; Ottawa makes back-to-back playoff appearances for first time in 12 years.Western ConferenceDallas Stars (C2) vs. Minnesota Wild (C3): The second first round meeting in four years for these Central Division counterparts.Vegas Golden Knights (P1) vs. Utah Mammoth (WC1): Golden Knights win their fifth Pacific Division title in nine years as the Mammoth make their playoff debut in their second season as a franchise.Which NHL teams have been eliminated from playoffs?There are 16 teams, eight in each conference, that have been eliminated from playoff contention.Here's a list of every team that will miss the 2025-26 Stanley Cup playoffs:Eastern ConferenceNew York RangersNew Jersey DevilsNew York IslandersDetroit Red WingsWashington CapitalsColumbus Blue JacketsToronto Maple LeafsFlorida PanthersWestern ConferenceNashville PredatorsSan Jose SharksSt. Louis BluesWinnipeg JetsSeattle KrakenCalgary FlamesChicago BlackhawksVancouver CanucksWhen is the final day of NHL season?The NHL regular season ends on Thursday, April 16.What NHL teams play today?Here's the NHL schedule for Thursday, April 16, with 12 teams in action as six Western Conference matchups will conclude the regular season.How can I watch NHL playoffs 2026TV: ESPN, ABC and TNT will broadcast all of the Stanley Cup playoff games in the United States.Watch NHL Stanley Cup playoffs live on FuboWhen do the NHL Stanley Cup playoffs start?While there's no official date just yet, the NHL is expected to announce the league's playoff schedule on the final day of the regular season, Thursday, April 16, with anticipation of the first round getting underway on Saturday, April 18.When is 2026 Stanley Cup Final?The exact dates for the Stanley Cup Final is still yet to be determined. Looking at recent history, it's a safe bet that the Stanley Cup Final will start in early June, usually within the first couple of days or week of June dating back the last three years since the Stanley Cup Final between the Vegas Golden Knights and Florida Panthers in 2023.When is the 2026 NHL Draft Lottery?The 2026 NHL Draft lottery is set for Tuesday, May 5.Who is the favorite to win Stanley Cup Final 2026? See oddsOdds according to BetMGM as of Wednesday, April 15:Here are the betting odds for all 16 playoff teams to lift Lord Stanley's Cup and be crowned as the new champions this June:Colorado Avalanche: 3/1 (+300)Carolina Hurricanes: 5/1 (+500)Tampa Bay Lightning: 5/1 (+500)Dallas Stars: 10/1 (+1000)Edmonton Oilers: 12/1 (+1200)Vegas Golden Knights: 12/1 (+1200)Minnesota Wild: 15/1 (+1500)Buffalo Sabres: 16/1 (+1600)Ottawa Senators: 20/1 (+2000)Pittsburgh Penguins: 22/1 (+2200)Montreal Canadiens: 25/1 (+2500)Utah Mammoth: 40/1 (+4000)Anaheim Ducks: 60/1 (+6000)Boston Bruins: 60/1 (+6000)Los Angeles Kings: 60/1 (+6000)Philadelphia Flyers: 60/1 (+6000)",
